within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.N_NervousSystem.N05B_Anxiolytics.N05BA01_Diazepam;
model Diazepam_Visser2003_PD_eeg
  "emax exposure-response sweep — Visser_2003 :: EEG (amplitude in the β-frequency band of the EEG)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 9.9,      // [V]
    Emax = 10.6,  // [V]
    EC50 = 0.000373,  // [kg/m3; ng·ml⁻¹ × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1.17,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng·ml⁻¹ per second
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 3800, Interval = 7.6),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Diazepam_Visser2003_PD_eeg</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Visser SA et al., <i>The Journal of pharmacology and experimental therapeutics 304(1):88–101</i> 2003 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1124/jpet.102.042341\">doi:10.1124/jpet.102.042341</a>) — amplitude in the β-frequency band of the EEG [V] against diazepam ng·ml⁻¹ — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =        9.9 V        drug-free response (baseline) (no-drug response, Q324)
  Emax  =       10.6 V        maximal effect term (intrinsic activity, Q320)
  EC50  =        373 ng·ml⁻¹  exposure at half of the maximal effect term (potency, Q321)
  gamma =       1.17          Hill coefficient (slope factor, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng·ml⁻¹ of diazepam per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 9.9   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (373 ng·ml⁻¹)  response 15.2
  exposure -> infinity  response 20.5</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Visser_2003: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Diazepam_Visser2003_PD_eeg;
